> # llama-cpp-rdna-boosts A patch collection that brings **AMD RDNA-specific performance work** to [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp): MTP decode, chunked gated-delta-net prefill, BF16 KV and WMMA flash-attention, fused MoE and k-quant decode paths, a hybrid all-reduce, qwen4exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) support, and an attention-memory campaign that frees several GiB of VRAM. It ships as **16 patches** (block 00 + blocks 01-15) for a clean llama.cpp checkout at the fork point **`790cf5 ... (truncated)
Based0.06.015.009 I sched_graph_realloc: graph reallocation: nodes = 4149 (changed = 0), splits = 26, n_same = 6, n_diff = 0
 on the documentation provided, here is a structured summary and guide for using the **llama-cpp-rdna-boosts** patch collection.

### 🚀 Overview
This project provides a collection of **16 patches** (`block 00` + `blocks 01-15`) designed to significantly boost performance on **AMD RDNA3, RDNA3.5, and RDNA4** GPUs within `llama.cpp`. It focuses on optimizing prefill, decode, and memory usage through specialized kernels and architectural fixes.

